---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/practical-solution-defense-tax.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — a New Defense-Funding Tax Measure" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why a \"Practical Solution,\" Not a Full Accounting Standard" },
        { id: "s4", label: "What \"Tentative Treatment\" Signals" },
        { id: "s5", label: "The General Practice of Tentative Practical Solutions for New Tax Measures" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Applying a Tentative Practical Solution" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="callout warn callout--centered">STATUS NOTE: Confirmed issued by the ASBJ on February 27, 2026 as a "Practical Solution" — a narrower, often TENTATIVE or transitional document type (distinct from a full Accounting Standard), explicitly labelled here as addressing "tentative treatment." Its precise substantive content beyond this general characterisation should be verified against ASBJ's current published materials.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a><a href="#s2">2. Scope — a New Defense-Funding Tax Measure</a><a href="#s3">3. Why a "Practical Solution," Not a Full Accounting Standard</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. What "Tentative Treatment" Signals</a><a href="#s5">5. The General Practice of Tentative Practical Solutions for New Tax Measures</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Worked Example — Applying a Tentative Practical Solution</a><a href="#s7">7. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</a><a href="#s9">9. Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Statement Mapping</a><a href="#s11">11. Related Standards</a><a href="#s12">12. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Interim guidance for a newly introduced, narrow tax measure</div>
        <div class="principle">This Practical Solution provides GUIDANCE for accounting for and DISCLOSING Japan's "SPECIAL CORPORATE TAX FOR DEFENSE" (防衛特別法人税) — a NEWLY introduced corporate tax measure connected to Japan's INCREASED defense spending — issued on a TENTATIVE basis, REFLECTING that detailed practical questions arising from a BRAND-NEW tax measure are often addressed THROUGH this narrower document type FIRST, PENDING fuller integration into the general tax accounting standards (ASBJ Statements No. 27 and No. 28) if and when WARRANTED.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — a New Defense-Funding Tax Measure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Companies subject to Japan's special corporate tax for defense</div>
        <div class="principle">This guidance applies to companies SUBJECT to Japan's special corporate tax FOR DEFENSE — a measure introduced as PART of the broader Japanese government's response to INCREASED defense budget requirements, ADDING to the existing layered tax system already addressed by ASBJ Statement No. 27 (Current Income Taxes — see the companion poster).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Why a "Practical Solution," Not a Full Accounting Standard</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A narrower, faster-issued document type for urgent, specific questions</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">"PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS" (実務対応報告) are a DISTINCT, NARROWER document type WITHIN the ASBJ's OUTPUT — typically addressing a SPECIFIC, often URGENT practical question (frequently arising from a NEW law or regulation) MORE QUICKLY than the FULL due-process cycle a comprehensive Accounting Standard would require. A NEWLY introduced tax measure, such as this defense-funding tax, is a TYPICAL trigger for this document TYPE — GIVING preparers TIMELY guidance WITHOUT waiting for a FULL Statement-level project.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>What "Tentative Treatment" Signals</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Guidance subject to potential future refinement</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The EXPLICIT use of "TENTATIVE" in this document's title signals that the ASBJ RECOGNISES the guidance may need FURTHER refinement as the tax LAW's practical application becomes CLEARER over time, or as related legislative DETAILS are finalised — a PRUDENT, transparent approach to providing TIMELY guidance for a genuinely NEW, evolving tax measure WITHOUT overstating the guidance's PERMANENCE.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The General Practice of Tentative Practical Solutions for New Tax Measures</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A recurring ASBJ response to significant new tax legislation</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">This APPROACH — issuing a TENTATIVE Practical Solution PROMPTLY following significant new tax LEGISLATION — MIRRORS how the ASBJ has PREVIOUSLY responded to OTHER major new tax developments (for example, GUIDANCE addressing the treatment of Japan's implementation of the OECD's GLOBAL MINIMUM TAX rules) — a RECURRING, well-established ASBJ practice of providing TIMELY, PRACTICAL guidance for SIGNIFICANT new tax measures AHEAD of any eventual FULL integration into the general tax accounting standards.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying a Tentative Practical Solution</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Recognising a new tax liability under interim guidance</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A company subject to the new defense tax measure</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company determines it is subject to the special corporate tax for defense for the current fiscal year, following the newly introduced tax measure.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company applies this Practical Solution's TENTATIVE guidance to determine the APPROPRIATE recognition and disclosure treatment for the resulting tax liability — while remaining ALERT to the possibility that FURTHER ASBJ refinement of this guidance MAY follow as the tax measure's practical application matures.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What this Practical Solution addresses</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Recognition and measurement of the special corporate tax for defense liability</span>
          <span>Disclosure of the nature and tentative basis of the accounting treatment applied</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Whether an entity is subject to the special corporate tax for defense, and how it interacts with existing enterprise/corporation tax treatment</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Estimated tax liability under a newly introduced, still-evolving tax measure</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely Japan-specific tax policy development</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">LIKE the SIZE-BASED enterprise tax classification question addressed in ASBJ Statement No. 27 (see the companion poster), this special defense-funding tax is a GENUINELY Japan-SPECIFIC tax policy development, WITHOUT a direct IFRS or US GAAP counterpart of the SAME type — NEITHER IAS 12 nor ASC 740 addresses a comparable NATIONAL defense-funding surtax construct.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where this new tax event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Special corporate tax for defense liability</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised per this Practical Solution's tentative guidance</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 27</span><span>Current Income Taxes — the general framework this Practical Solution supplements for the new defense tax measure</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 28</span><span>Tax Effect Accounting — relevant if the new tax measure gives rise to any deferred tax consequences</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Practical Solution (実務対応報告)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A narrower, often more quickly issued ASBJ document type addressing specific practical questions, frequently arising from new laws or regulations.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Special corporate tax for defense</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A newly introduced Japanese corporate tax measure connected to increased national defense spending.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
        <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
        <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
        <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
